# E15: git's own checkout-time newline translation (`core.autocrlf=true` on
# this Windows checkout) is what re-introduces CRLF into the JSON manifests
# Prettier wants as LF (`apps/desktop/package.json`,
# `apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json`) every time the tree is cloned or
# reset, even after `scripts/sync_version.py` and `make format` both agree
# on LF. `text=auto` lets git normalize line endings for anything it
# detects as text; the explicit `eol=lf` rules below pin the file types
# `apps/desktop`'s Prettier config actually reformats to LF specifically, so
# that normalization never flips them back to CRLF on this platform.
* text=auto

apps/desktop/**/*.json text eol=lf
apps/desktop/**/*.ts text eol=lf
apps/desktop/**/*.tsx text eol=lf
apps/desktop/**/*.md text eol=lf
